[Music]  kate middleton is showing off her  impressive piano skills  [Music]  during the royal carols together at  christmas concert special held at  westminster abbey the duchess of  cambridge debuted her surprising music  talent yup that's the royal on the piano  rocking a red dress for the special  occasion alongside scottish singer tom  walker the two performed his song for  those who can't be here  [Music]  this marks the duchess's first ever  public piano performance not only were  fans around the world impressed so was  walker who had this sweet reaction to  their duet on twitter just  one of those pinch yourself  crazy moments playing your song with the  member of the royal family is definitely  not your everyday occurrence so yeah i  just want to say a huge thank you  uh to the duchess of cambridge and to  the whole royal family for having me  be a small part of such an amazing  service turns out this moment was very  special for kate too ahead of the event  she reflected on the past year and  opened up about the importance of coming  together we've seen so many challenges  we've lost our loved ones we've seen our  frontline workers under immense pressure  and also we've been more emotionally and  socially distanced and isolated from  each other but i suppose through that  separation we've also realized how much  we need each other and how acts of  kindness and love can really bring us  comfort and relief in times of distress  and part of that comfort is celebrating  the holidays earlier this month kate and  her hubby prince william shared this  cute christmas card featuring their  family that's the two posing alongside  their children eight-year-old prince  george six-year-old princess charlotte  and three-year-old prince louis as for  how the royal celebrated the holidays  well just last week a source close to  the family told et quote prince william  and kate have been scheduled to stay at  anmer hall located on the sandringham  estate with their three kids adding they  have spent years past with kate's  parents in bucklebury berkshire which is  near windsor castle details are still  being worked out on how the move to  windsor castle will adjust christmas  plans and when it comes to william's  brother prince harry and his wife meghan  markle seems there's still tension  between the families following harry and  megan's decision to step back from their  royal duties and their tell-all  interview with oprah winfrey earlier  this year back in july royal expert  katie nicholl told et when she thinks  the brothers will be together again well  we don't know when we'll next see the  brothers together i think the idea of  christmases together is probably  not likely to happen this year of course  the covered pandemic does mean that  international travel is more challenging  i think we can be certain that harry and  megan will be coming back to britain i  think the platinum jubilee celebrations  in june 2022  are a likely opportunity for them to  come over to be a part of the official  celebrations of the queen's 70th year

